conditional statement to write the equivalence as a conjunction of implications: \n\n$$\n¬(R⇔S)≡¬((R⇒S)∧(S⇒R))\n$$\n\nNow, we represent all the implications using disjunctions and negations:\n\n$$\n¬((R⇒S)∧(S⇒R))≡¬((¬R∨S)∧(¬S∨R))\n$$\n\nNext, we use De Morgan's laws:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬((¬R∨S)∧(¬S∨R)) & ≡¬(¬R∨S)∨¬(¬S∨R) \\\\  & ≡(¬¬R∧¬S)∨(¬¬S∧¬R)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the double negations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(¬¬R∧¬S)∨(¬¬S∧¬R) & ≡(R∧¬S)∨(S∧¬R)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378740 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378740 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378740 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378740 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378740 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378740 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378740 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378740 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186378741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378740 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fa635f77-ae2d-55de-9a31-bd8bedcbba5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378741 #edb/ref 1080 "(R∧¬S)∨(S∧¬R)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378741 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378741 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2a5ead25-f894-5c56-8fc8-208d6efb2411" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378742 #edb/ref 1080 "(R∨¬S)∧(S∧¬R)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378742 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378742 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4e44a41f-1278-545b-a105-bae7c0bc610d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378743 #edb/ref 1080 "(¬R∧S)∨(¬S∨R)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378743 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378743 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c76a143-fa4b-5a2d-93e7-c167938193a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921863